Do not share the model file's mmap fd with NNAPI drivers.

With mmap sharing enabled, the NNAPI delegate passes the mmapped model
file's descriptor to the driver inside the compilation request. Our
models live on external storage (fuse), which vendor HAL processes are
not allowed to read: on the Pixel 9 Pro the kernel's binder SELinux hook
rejects transferring the fd (avc denied { read } for dev="fuse"
scontext=u:r:hal_neuralnetworks_darwinn), getSupportedOperations fails
with FAILED_TRANSACTION, and the whole graph silently falls back to CPU.
Master's TF 2.18 build never passes a file fd on this path (its device
runs show no such denials), so disable the fd-sharing block and let the
delegate copy weights; the NNAPI runtime then stages them in ashmem
pools, which vendor HALs may map.

--- a/tensorflow/lite/delegates/nnapi/nnapi_delegate.cc
+++ b/tensorflow/lite/delegates/nnapi/nnapi_delegate.cc
@@ -48,7 +48,6 @@
 #endif
 
 #if defined __ANDROID__ || defined __unix__
-#define TFLITE_NNAPI_ALLOW_MMAP_SHARING
 #include <sys/mman.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #endif
